---
// THE OPENING. The FS mark as 5,000 glowing points, scroll-driven into an explosion that
// hands the page over to the hero video. Adrian dialled every number in a local harness
// (MrMiata: workspace/website/2026-08-18_point-cloud-hero/build) and they are transcribed
// here verbatim; nothing in this file is an implementer's choice.
//
// This is the FIRST client-side JavaScript the site has ever shipped, which is why it is
// hand-rolled WebGL2 rather than three.js: the alternative was 150-200 KB plus a GLB
// download to draw 5,000 dots. The mark never changes, so its geometry is baked at build
// time (MrMiata: build/bake.py) into a 9 KB positions+normals+indices binary, and the
// even-surface sampling runs once on load from a fixed seed.
//
// It is progressive enhancement over the static markup below it. Reduced motion, no WebGL2,
// or a failed init all leave the copy standing on carbon, and the scroll runway collapses so
// nobody scrolls through three empty screens to reach the page.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BracketButton from './BracketButton.astro';
import heroWordmark from '../assets/hero/wordmark-banner.png';
---

{/* THE STAGE IS A STACK OF FIXED LAYERS (Adrian, 2026-08-19). Nothing scrolls past anything:
    scroll position is just the clock, and the layers fade and move against it in place.
      z0  the 3D scene (canvas: grid + cloud), never scrolls away
      z1  the hero video, which FADES IN over the scene as the cloud explodes (the section
          itself, promoted to a fixed layer by [data-cine] in index.astro)
      z2  this copy layer: text that clears on beat one, and the two download buttons, which
          never fade at all -- they travel to centre-bottom and STAY, above the video
      higher  the nav */}
<div class="pc" data-pc>
  <div class="pc__stage">
    <canvas class="pc__canvas" data-pc-canvas aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="pc__copylayer">
  <div class="pc__copy">
    <div class="pc__text" data-pc-text>
      <p class="pc__display">Artist+AI Toolset</p>
      <p class="pc__sub">Game Development<br />Re-imagined.</p>
      {/* The wordmark stays the h1, as it was before this section existed, so the page's
          heading shape is unchanged. Its vertical offset is set once at load to sit on the
          crossbar of the F in the point cloud (Adrian's alignment, 2026-08-19). */}
      <h1 class="pc__wordmark" data-pc-wordmark>
        <Image src={heroWordmark} alt="FabricatorStudio" widths={[760, 1180]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 86vw, 760px" loading="eager" />
      </h1>
    </div>
    {/* The buttons never fade (Adrian, 2026-08-19): they travel to centre-bottom as the
        camera centres, then hold there, above the video, for as long as the stage is on
        screen. The ask outlives the whole opening. That is why they sit outside .pc__text,
        which owns the text fade, and on a layer above the video's z1. */}
    <div class="pc__cta" data-pc-cta>
      <BracketButton kind="hard" installer label="Download Toolset" event="hero-download" />
      <BracketButton kind="plasma-outline" href="/armature/" label="Download Armature" event="hero-armature" />
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* THE PHILOSOPHY (Adrian, 2026-08-19): fades in when the camera lands at beat B, centred
      above the download buttons, and STAYS up through the video. This is his own rewrite of
      2026-08-01, moved from the old video-hero copy block; the emphasis markup is carried
      over verbatim, owner's override on the "These are not AI tools" shape included. */}
  <div class="pc__philosophy">
    {/* Stepped, not simultaneous (Adrian, 2026-08-19): the studio line stands with the mark
        at beat B, then hands off to the refinement line as the video fades in. They occupy
        the same grid cell so the swap happens in place rather than reflowing. */}
    <p class="pc__phil-lead" style="opacity: var(--phil1, 0)"><b>FabricatorStudio is a one-person Technical Art studio making Artist Driven AI tools.</b> <b class="pc__phil-hl">Free for small studios.</b></p>
    <p class="pc__phil-line" style="opacity: var(--phil2, 0)">Most AI tooling is built without refinement in mind. <b>FabricatorStudio tools are built so you can <b class="pc__phil-ember">drive your asset to production level standards</b>.</b></p>
  </div>
</div>

{/* The scroll the whole stage is spent on. Purely a clock: the OPENING owns the first 1.6
    screens of scroll (its beat fractions are ruled against exactly that length, so it never
    changes when the runway grows), the TOOLSET's glass-and-carousel entry owns the next 1.2,
    then each of the remaining five tools takes 0.4 screens as a SNAPPED STEP, the ARMATURE
    beat takes over from 4.8 screens (carousel out, Armature in by 5.4), and the last 0.4 is
    its hold. 100svh viewport + 5.8 scroll screens = 680svh. */}
<div class="pc-runway" data-pc-runway></div>

<style>
  .pc {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    /* The nav sits over this; the panels sit over it too. Nothing here ever takes a click. */
    pointer-events: none;
    background: var(--carbon);
  }
  .pc__stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; }
  /* svh, not vh: on mobile vh measures the viewport with the toolbars retracted, so a runway
     in vh is taller than what you can see and the beat timing drifts as the URL bar collapses. */
  .pc-runway { height: 680svh; }

  /* The copy rides its own fixed layer ABOVE the video's z1, because the buttons must stay
     clickable and visible after the video has faded in underneath them. */
  .pc__copylayer {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    /* 3, not 2: the toolset glass lives at 2 and the buttons must stand ON it, sharp,
       never blurred under it. */
    z-index: 3;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .pc__canvas {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    /* Nothing to look at until the cloud has been sampled and drawn once. */
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 400ms var(--ease-out);
  }
  .pc__canvas[data-ready] { opacity: 1; }

  .pc__copy {
    position: absolute;
    left: 9vw;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    max-width: 44vw;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    /* The layer is click-through; the buttons are the one thing that takes a click. The
       faded-out text must NOT: pointer-events comes back on the CTA row only. */
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .pc__cta :global(a) { pointer-events: auto; }

  /* Centred above the buttons' landing spot, driven by --phil-in from the loop. Text over
     moving footage with no scrim, so the shadow is what keeps it legible on a bright frame. */
  .pc__philosophy {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    bottom: calc(8% + 6.5rem);
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: min(52rem, 86vw);
    text-align: center;
    pointer-events: none;
    text-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(11, 14, 16, 0.65);
    /* Both paragraphs share one cell: the handoff is a crossfade in place, never a reflow. */
    display: grid;
  }
  .pc__philosophy > p { grid-area: 1 / 1; align-self: end; }
  /* Same register as the opening's "Game Development Re-imagined." line (Adrian,
     2026-08-19): the two beats speak at one size. */
  .pc__phil-lead,
  .pc__phil-line {
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.22;
    color: var(--bone);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.3vw, 2.05rem);
  }

  .pc__philosophy b { color: var(--bone); font-weight: 700; }
  .pc__philosophy .pc__phil-hl { color: var(--plasma); }
  .pc__philosophy .pc__phil-ember { color: var(--ember); }

  /* The fade lives here and not on .pc__copy, because a child cannot be more opaque than its
     parent and the buttons have to outlive the text. */
  .pc__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    opacity: calc(1 - var(--pc-out, 0));
    transform: translateY(calc(var(--pc-out, 0) * -24px));
  }

  .pc__display {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5.2vw, 5rem);
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  .pc__sub {
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.22;
    color: var(--bone);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.3vw, 2.05rem);
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }

  /* position/top and NOT a margin: the offset that sits this on the F's crossbar must not
     change the copy column's height, because the column's height is what the mark's framing
     was set against. */
  .pc__wordmark {
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0;
    position: relative;
    top: var(--pc-wm, 0px);
  }
  .pc__wordmark :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: min(34vw, 470px);
    height: auto;
  }

  .pc__cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 3.4rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    will-change: transform, opacity;
  }

  /* ---- the fallback -------------------------------------------------------------------
     Reduced motion, no WebGL2, or a failed init: the canvas layer goes entirely, the copy
     layer drops into the flow as an ordinary opening screen on carbon, and the runway
     collapses so nobody scrolls two and a half empty screens to reach the page. The video
     section keeps its normal in-flow life because [data-cine] is never set. */
  .pc[data-pc-static] { display: none; }
  .pc[data-pc-static] ~ .pc__copylayer {
    position: relative;
    inset: auto;
    pointer-events: auto;
    min-height: calc(100svh - var(--header-h));
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .pc[data-pc-static] ~ .pc__copylayer .pc__philosophy {
    position: relative;
    left: 0;
    bottom: auto;
    transform: none;
    width: auto;
    max-width: min(44rem, 82vw);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0 9vw;
    text-align: left;
    text-shadow: none;
    display: block;
  }
  .pc[data-pc-static] ~ .pc__copylayer .pc__philosophy > p { opacity: 1 !important; }
  .pc[data-pc-static] ~ .pc__copylayer .pc__phil-line { margin-top: 0.9rem; }
  .pc[data-pc-static] ~ .pc__copylayer .pc__copy {
    position: relative;
    top: auto;
    left: 0;
    transform: none;
    max-width: min(44rem, 82vw);
    margin-left: 9vw;
    padding: var(--sp-7) 0;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }
  .pc[data-pc-static] ~ .pc__copylayer .pc__text { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .pc[data-pc-static] ~ .pc__copylayer .pc__wordmark { top: 0; }
  .pc[data-pc-static] ~ .pc-runway { display: none; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    /* Mobile is composed but NOT dialled: Adrian ruled the layout (mark toward the top, copy
       in the lower third, buttons at the bottom) and deferred its camera. Until that framing
       exists this width takes the static fallback rather than an undialled cinematic. */
    .pc { display: none; }
    .pc__copylayer { position: relative; inset: auto; pointer-events: auto; min-height: calc(100svh - var(--header-h)); display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: flex-start; }
    .pc__philosophy { position: relative; left: 0; bottom: auto; transform: none; width: auto; margin: 1.25rem 0 0 0; padding: 0 var(--container-px, 20px); text-align: left; text-shadow: none; display: block; }
    .pc__philosophy > p { opacity: 1 !important; }
    .pc__phil-line { margin-top: 0.9rem; }
    .pc__copy { position: relative; top: auto; transform: none; left: 0; margin: 0; max-width: none; padding: var(--sp-7) var(--container-px, 20px); pointer-events: auto; }
    .pc__text { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    .pc__wordmark { top: 0; }
    .pc__wordmark :global(img) { width: min(86vw, 470px); }
    .pc-runway { display: none; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- the ruled numbers
  // Transcribed from Adrian's harness. Do not tune these here; tune them there and copy back.
  const P = {
    count: 5000, seed: 1, size: 0.0356,
    freq: 3, rip: 2, freq2: 1, rip2: 5.3, mix2: 0.1,
    oscLow: 0.008, oscHigh: 0.855, oscSpeed: 0.1, oscShape: 1.45, oscAttack: 0.175,
    cFreq: 0.35, cSpread: 0.06, fadeDepth: 0,
    bloomStrength: 2.4, bloomRadius: 0.34, bloomThreshold: 0.3, bloomKnee: 0.15,
    gridOpacity: 1, fogNear: 2.0, fogFar: 14.0,
    exDist: 1.5, exCurl: 2.16, exCam: 1.06,
    restAmp: 0.012, wakeAt: 0.04,
    anchorY: 0.415, ctaBottom: 0.08,
    // The star shell (Adrian, 2026-08-19): environment, indifferent to the beats. Dim enough
    // that only the brightest twinkle just past the bloom threshold.
    // Sizes vary per star, 0.02-0.1 (Adrian, 2026-08-19), biased small so a handful of big
    // ones carry the presence and the rest carry the depth.
    starCount: 2600, starSizeMin: 0.02, starSizeMax: 0.35, starSpeed: 0.015, starBright: 1.0,
  };
  const CAM_A = { yaw: -0.0200, pitch: -0.0240, dist: 4.36448, tx: -0.62800, ty: 0.89876, tz: -0.83070, fov: 42 };
  const CAM_B = { yaw: -0.0320, pitch: -0.1160, dist: 3.14928, tx: 0.08734, ty: 0.79470, tz: 0.00000, fov: 42 };

  const root = document.querySelector('[data-pc]') as HTMLElement | null;
  if (root) start(root);

  function fallback(el: HTMLElement) {
    el.setAttribute('data-pc-static', '');
    // If init died after the video was promoted to a fixed layer, un-promote it, or the page
    // is left with an invisible fixed video and no hero at all.
    const hero = document.getElementById('hero');
    if (hero) { hero.removeAttribute('data-cine'); hero.style.opacity = ''; }
  }

  async function start(host: HTMLElement) {
    const reduced = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    const narrow = matchMedia('(max-width: 900px)').matches;
    if (reduced || narrow) { fallback(host); return; }

    const canvas = host.querySelector('[data-pc-canvas]') as HTMLCanvasElement;
    const gl = canvas.getContext('webgl2', { antialias: true, alpha: false });
    if (!gl) { fallback(host); return; }

    try { await run(host, canvas, gl); }
    catch (err) {
      // NEVER silent: a swallowed init error demotes the whole opening to the static page
      // with no trace, which cost a debugging round on 2026-08-19.
      console.error('[pointcloud] init failed, static fallback:', err);
      fallback(host);
    }
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------- maths
  const sub = (a: number[], b: number[]) => [a[0] - b[0], a[1] - b[1], a[2] - b[2]];
  const dot = (a: number[], b: number[]) => a[0] * b[0] + a[1] * b[1] + a[2] * b[2];
  const cross = (a: number[], b: number[]) => [a[1] * b[2] - a[2] * b[1], a[2] * b[0] - a[0] * b[2], a[0] * b[1] - a[1] * b[0]];
  const norm = (a: number[]) => { const l = Math.hypot(a[0], a[1], a[2]) || 1; return [a[0] / l, a[1] / l, a[2] / l]; };
  const lerp = (a: number, b: number, t: number) => a + (b - a) * t;
  const clamp01 = (t: number) => Math.min(1, Math.max(0, t));
  const smooth = (t: number) => t * t * (3 - 2 * t);

  function perspective(fovDeg: number, aspect: number, near: number, far: number) {
    const f = 1 / Math.tan((fovDeg * Math.PI / 180) / 2), nf = 1 / (near - far);
    return new Float32Array([f / aspect, 0, 0, 0, 0, f, 0, 0, 0, 0, (far + near) * nf, -1, 0, 0, 2 * far * near * nf, 0]);
  }
  function lookAt(eye: number[], target: number[], up: number[]) {
    const z = norm(sub(eye, target)), x = norm(cross(up, z)), y = cross(z, x);
    return new Float32Array([
      x[0], y[0], z[0], 0, x[1], y[1], z[1], 0, x[2], y[2], z[2], 0,
      -dot(x, eye), -dot(y, eye), -dot(z, eye), 1]);
  }
  // Deterministic: Adrian tuned against ONE cloud, so an unseeded sample would be a slightly
  // different cloud on every machine.
  function mulberry32(a: number) {
    return function () {
      a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6D2B79F5) | 0;
      let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);
      t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;
      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;
    };
  }

  async function run(host: HTMLElement, canvas: HTMLCanvasElement, gl: WebGL2RenderingContext) {
    const HDR = gl.getExtension('EXT_color_buffer_float') ? gl.RGBA16F : gl.RGBA8;
    gl.getExtension('OES_texture_float_linear');

    const sh = (type: number, src: string) => {
      const s = gl.createShader(type)!; gl.shaderSource(s, src); gl.compileShader(s);
      if (!gl.getShaderParameter(s, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(s) || 'shader');
      return s;
    };
    const prog = (vs: string, fs: string) => {
      const p = gl.createProgram()!;
      gl.attachShader(p, sh(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, vs)); gl.attachShader(p, sh(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, fs));
      gl.linkProgram(p);
      if (!gl.getProgramParameter(p, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(p) || 'link');
      const u: Record<string, WebGLUniformLocation | null> = {};
      const n = gl.getProgramParameter(p, gl.ACTIVE_UNIFORMS);
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        const nm = gl.getActiveUniform(p, i)!.name.replace('[0]', '');
        u[nm] = gl.getUniformLocation(p, nm);
      }
      return { p, u };
    };
    const target = (w: number, h: number, fmt: number) => {
      const t = gl.createTexture()!;
      gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, t);
      gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, fmt, w, h, 0, gl.RGBA, fmt === gl.RGBA16F ? gl.HALF_FLOAT : gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, null);
      gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);
      gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);
      gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
      gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);
      const f = gl.createFramebuffer()!;
      gl.bindFramebuffer(gl.FRAMEBUFFER, f);
      gl.framebufferTexture2D(gl.FRAMEBUFFER, gl.COLOR_ATTACHMENT0, gl.TEXTURE_2D, t, 0);
      gl.bindFramebuffer(gl.FRAMEBUFFER, null);
      return { f, t, w, h };
    };

    // ---- shaders. The prototype's, unchanged in behaviour.
    const POINT_VS = `#version 300 es
in vec3 aPos; in vec3 aNor; in float aPhase; in float aPhase2; in vec3 aRand;
uniform mat4 uProj, uView;
uniform float uTime, uAmp, uFreq, uRip, uFreq2, uRip2, uMix2, uSize;
uniform float uCFreq, uCSpread, uFadeDepth;
uniform float uExplode, uExDist, uExCurl, uExCam;
uniform vec3 uCamDir;
out float vFade; out float vWave; out float vAlive;
void main() {
  // Two crossing waves MIXED rather than summed, so the blend changes the character of the
  // motion without changing how far the points travel.
  float w1 = sin(uTime * uFreq + aPhase * uRip);
  float w2 = sin(uTime * uFreq2 + aPhase2 * uRip2);
  float w = mix(w1, w2, uMix2);
  vec3 p = aPos + aNor * (w * uAmp);
  // The explosion is a pluck that never comes back: same snap, but the point keeps its
  // velocity. Direction is seeded per point, never radial, because radial reads as fireworks.
  if (uExplode > 0.0) {
    float e = uExplode;
    vec3 dir = normalize(mix(normalize(aRand * 2.0 - 1.0), aNor, 0.35) + uCamDir * uExCam);
    vec3 curl = normalize(cross(dir, aNor + vec3(0.0, 0.001, 0.0)));
    p += dir * (e * e * uExDist) + curl * (sin(e * 3.14159 + aPhase) * e * uExCurl);
  }
  vec4 mv = uView * vec4(p, 1.0);
  gl_Position = uProj * mv;
  // Point size is a PIXEL size, not a world size, against this exact scaling.
  gl_PointSize = uSize * (300.0 / -mv.z);
  vFade = 1.0 - uFadeDepth * 0.9 * (0.5 - 0.5 * w);
  vWave = sin(uTime * uCFreq + aPhase * uRip * uCSpread);
  vAlive = 1.0 - uExplode * 0.65;
}`;

    const POINT_FS = `#version 300 es
precision highp float;
uniform vec3 uPlasma, uEmber, uBone;
in float vFade; in float vWave; in float vAlive;
out vec4 frag;
void main() {
  vec2 d = gl_PointCoord - vec2(0.5);
  float r = dot(d, d);
  if (r > 0.25) discard;
  float soft = smoothstep(0.25, 0.0, r);
  // Bone at the wave's midpoint, Plasma at one crest and Ember at the other.
  vec3 c = vWave > 0.0 ? mix(uBone, uPlasma, vWave) : mix(uBone, uEmber, -vWave);
  frag = vec4(c * vFade, soft * vAlive);
}`;

    // Stars: a slow uniform orbit around Y, done in the shader so the buffer never updates.
    // aSeed.x is a twinkle phase, aSeed.y a per-star brightness.
    const STAR_VS = `#version 300 es
in vec3 aPos; in vec3 aSeed;
uniform mat4 uProj, uView; uniform float uTime, uSpeed;
out float vB;
void main() {
  float a = uTime * uSpeed;
  float c = cos(a), s = sin(a);
  vec3 p = vec3(aPos.x * c - aPos.z * s, aPos.y, aPos.x * s + aPos.z * c);
  vec4 mv = uView * vec4(p, 1.0);
  gl_Position = uProj * mv;
  // aSeed.z is this star's own size; the floor keeps the far small ones from flickering out.
  gl_PointSize = max(aSeed.z * (300.0 / -mv.z), 1.0);
  vB = aSeed.y * (0.75 + 0.25 * sin(uTime * 0.6 + aSeed.x));
}`;

    const STAR_FS = `#version 300 es
precision highp float;
uniform vec3 uBone; uniform float uBright;
in float vB; out vec4 frag;
void main() {
  vec2 d = gl_PointCoord - vec2(0.5);
  float r = dot(d, d);
  if (r > 0.25) discard;
  frag = vec4(uBone * vB * uBright, smoothstep(0.25, 0.0, r));
}`;

    const GRID_VS = `#version 300 es
in vec3 aPos; uniform mat4 uProj, uView; out float vDist;
void main() { vec4 mv = uView * vec4(aPos, 1.0); vDist = -mv.z; gl_Position = uProj * mv; }`;

    const GRID_FS = `#version 300 es
precision highp float;
uniform vec3 uColor, uFogColor; uniform float uOpacity, uFogNear, uFogFar;
in float vDist; out vec4 frag;
void main() {
  float f = clamp((uFogFar - vDist) / (uFogFar - uFogNear), 0.0, 1.0);
  frag = vec4(mix(uFogColor, uColor, f), uOpacity * f);
}`;

    const QUAD_VS = `#version 300 es
in vec2 aPos; out vec2 vUv;
void main() { vUv = aPos * 0.5 + 0.5; gl_Position = vec4(aPos, 0.0, 1.0); }`;

    // Threshold 0 blooms everything, which was right over an empty void and wrong the moment
    // the grid existed: the floor glowed.
    const BRIGHT_FS = `#version 300 es
precision highp float;
uniform sampler2D uTex; uniform float uThreshold, uKnee;
in vec2 vUv; out vec4 frag;
void main() {
  vec3 c = texture(uTex, vUv).rgb;
  float l = dot(c, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722));
  frag = vec4(c * smoothstep(uThreshold, uThreshold + uKnee, l), 1.0);
}`;

